@page "/combined"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Combined — GGNet Demo</PageTitle>

<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Combined features</h1>

<p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-gray-600">
    Everything shipped so far on one chart: host buttons drive the view window
    through @@ref commands, the wheel zooms about the cursor, the crosshair
    reads out the time axis, and double-click resets — all reconciling
    last-writer-wins on the same view state.
</p>

<div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
    <button class="rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-gray-100" @onclick=ZoomToMidWeekAsync>Zoom: day 2–4</button>
    <button class="rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-gray-100" @onclick=ShowLastTwoDaysAsync>Last 48 h</button>
    <button class="rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-gray-100" @onclick=ResetAsync>Reset</button>
</div>

<div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
    <Plot @ref=plot Context=@context RenderMode=@renderMode Interactivity=@interactivity />
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Faceted</h2>

<p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-gray-600">
    The same gestures on a faceted plot: the view window lives on the
    plot-wide axis container, so wheel zoom in either panel windows both, and
    every re-instanced facet scale inherits it.
</p>

<div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
    <Plot Context=@facetedContext RenderMode=@renderMode Interactivity=@interactivity />
</div>
